{"user": "I think I just played 7b, but that square is now white. Why?", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T13:10:47.169435+00:00", "assistant": "Because in Othello, a disc you place can be flipped later.\n\nIf you played **b7** (column b, row 7), it was Black at that moment. On White\u2019s next move(s), if White made a straight line with White discs on both ends and your **b7** disc in between, **b7 gets flipped to White**.\n\nOnly **corner discs** are truly permanent; edge discs like **b7** can still be flipped until they become stable.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T13:10:51.769494+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T13:10:54.162375+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Worked Line": 2, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 2, "Board Report": 1}, "confidence": {"Worked Line": 0.6666666666666666, "General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666, "Board Report": 0.3333333