{"user": "explain my options now", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T13:15:53.884419+00:00", "assistant": "Your legal options are **a1, g2, a3**:\n\n- **a1**: takes a corner, which is permanent. But it may leave White a strong reply at **a3**, flipping the left edge.\n- **g2**: flips a lot now, but be careful: it can give White access to the **h1 corner**.\n- **a3**: not a corner, but it attacks White\u2019s mobility. After it, check whether White has *any* legal move \u2014 if not, White must **pass**, and you get another move.\n\nSo don\u2019t just count flips; ask: \u201cWhich move leaves White with the fewest replies?\u201d", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T13:16:19.723065+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T13:16:21.933896+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction", "Pose Simplified Problem"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction", "Pose Simplified Problem"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Prompt": 1, "Pose Simplified Problem": 3, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Prompt": 0.3333333333333333, "Pose Simplified Problem": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction", "Prompt", "Pose Simplified Problem"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction", "Pose Simplified Problem"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint", "Pose Simplified Problem"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"],